(SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE BOARD OF INDIA) Tj
T*
(ALTERNATIVE INVESTMENT FUND AND FOREIGN PORTFOLIO INVESTORS DEPARTMENT, MUMBAI) Tj
T*
(SEBI/HO/AFD/AFD-PoD-2/P/CIR/2024/160) Tj
T*
(September 27, 2024) Tj
T*
(Master Circular for Foreign Portfolio Investors \(FPIs\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Categorization of FPIs: Foreign Portfolio Investors are classified into two categories:) Tj
T*
(\(a\) Category I FPI: Government and government-related entities such as central banks, sovereign wealth funds, international agencies,) Tj
T*
(and regulated entities including pension funds and insurance funds from FATF-compliant jurisdictions.) Tj
T*
(\(b\) Category II FPI: Appropriately regulated funds, broad-based funds, university endowments, charitable trusts, and corporate bodies.) Tj
T*
(2. Individual and Group Holding Limits: The total investment by each Foreign Portfolio Investor or its investor group shall remain strictly) Tj
T*
(below ten percent \(10 percent\) of the total issued and paid-up equity share capital of a listed Indian company. If holdings touch or exceed) Tj
T*
(ten percent, the FPI must divest the excess within five trading days, failing which the entire holding is reclassified as Foreign Direct Investment \(FDI\).) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
9 0 obj
<< /Length 908 >>
stream
BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 720 Td
13 TL
(3. Granular Beneficial Ownership Disclosures: FPIs meeting either of the following concentration criteria must provide granular) Tj
T*
(disclosures identifying all natural persons holding economic interest or control:) Tj
T*
(\(i\) FPIs holding more than 50 percent of their total Indian equity Assets Under Management \(AUM\) in a single Indian corporate group; or) Tj
T*
(\(ii\) FPIs that individually, or along with their investor group, hold Indian equity AUM exceeding rupees twenty-five thousand crore \(INR 25,000 crore\).) Tj
T*
(Exemptions apply to sovereign wealth funds, public retail funds, and regulated ETFs.) Tj
T*
(4. Surrender of Registration: An FPI wishing to surrender its registration must liquidate all holdings and settle tax obligations within) Tj
T*
(30 business days of applying for surrender to the Designated Depository Participant \(DDP\).) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
10 0 obj
<< /Length 774 >>
stream
BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 720 Td
13 TL
(5. Offshore Derivative Instruments \(ODIs / P-Notes\): Only Category I FPIs may issue, subscribe to, or deal in Offshore Derivative) Tj
T*
(Instruments \(ODIs\). Issuance of ODIs to entities that are non-compliant with FATF standards or have opaque ownership structures is prohibited.) Tj
T*
(6. Prohibition of ODIs on Derivatives: FPIs shall not issue ODIs with derivative contracts as the underlying asset, except where such derivative) Tj
T*
(positions are entered into by the FPI purely for hedging equity holdings in Indian companies.) Tj
T*
(7. Custody and Clearing: All FPIs must appoint a SEBI-registered Custodian of Securities and enter into a custodial agreement prior to executing) Tj
T*
(any market transactions in India.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
11 0 obj
<< /Length 803 >>
stream
BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 720 Td
13 TL
(8. Investor Group Clubbing: Multiple FPI entities having common ownership of more than 50 percent or common control shall be treated as) Tj
T*
(a single investor group for the purpose of monitoring the 10 percent equity holding limit.) Tj
T*
(9. Divestment Timelines for Breaches: In the event of an inadvertent breach of the 10 percent limit due to corporate actions \(rights issue, buyback\),) Tj
T*
(the FPI group is granted five trading days to bring holdings below the threshold.) Tj
T*
(10. Periodic KYC Updation: FPIs must submit updated KYC records to their Designated Depository Participant \(DDP\) every three years for Category I) Tj
T*
(and every year for Category II.) Tj
T*
(Yours faithfully,) Tj
T*
(\(Sunil J. Kadam\)) Tj
T*
(Chief General Manager) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
